in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @time
in @void
in @void/narcissus
in @song
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/reality/time

# @time/past — backwards-lens temporal-projection species; the
# temporal projection of @void/narcissus through @song saga.
#
# First species-decl of the @time family (family-root marker landed
# same tick at `shards/time.mirror`). Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara per
# Alex Round 2 spawn brief.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# @time/past IS the substrate-decl'd temporal projection of the
# backwards-lens substrate-mode carried by @void/narcissus. Per
# @void/narcissus (Round-1 landing `shards/void/narcissus.mirror`):
# the backwards lens consumes H(t) — the observer's own past-
# trajectory — as its native input. @time/past IS that H(t)
# projection at temporal-family altitude, mediated through the
# @song saga.
#
# Carrier: `peer_history H(t)` — the ordered sequence of prior
# @song/beats the observer's timeline traversed. Content-addressed
# per `@epistemologic/property/verdict_is_content_addressed`
# discipline. The past is not opinion; the past is the content-
# addressed trace of settled beats.
#
# === Composition with @void/narcissus ===
#
# @void/narcissus's operational altitude is substrate-mode
# (backwards-lens as one pole of the void duality). @time/past's
# operational altitude is temporal-family (the temporal-projection
# of the same substrate-mode through the @song saga).
#
# Composition edge: @time/past.time_past_state.peer_history ==
# @void/narcissus.void_narcissus_state.peer_history at content-
# addressed identity. The two carriers name the SAME H(t) at
# different altitudes; one at substrate-mode altitude, one at
# temporal-family altitude.
#
# === Composition with @song saga ===
#
# @song saga (family-root at `shards/song.mirror`; @song/beat at
# `shards/song/beat.mirror`) is the SAGA COMMAND SURFACE through
# which @time projects. @time/past reads the saga's PRIOR beats —
# beats that have already crystallized (per Mara Round-2 Crystal/
# Mandelbrot landing) — as the H(t) it consumes.
#
# Each prior @song/beat is a Crystal<T> settled at some @time/now
# event; the sequence of Crystal<T> settlements IS the observer's
# peer_history H(t). @time/past's operational surface reads through
# the saga's prior-beats chain.
#
# === Förster invariant composition (Alex Round 2 Q3 ratified) ===
#
# The Förster invariant `pillar::choices_monotone_of_song` applies
# to @time/past as follows: reading the past MUST NOT REDUCE the
# choices available to peers in the present or future. A backwards-
# lens observation that COLLAPSES peer choice-sets (e.g., narrative-
# imposition; deterministic-past-forcing) violates the Förster
# invariant.
#
# The `past_reading_preserves_choices` bilateral (below) checks the
# Förster invariant at species altitude. Backwards-lens observation
# is admissible iff reading H(t) does not reduce the present-tick
# choice-set.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/time/past.mirror`.** Clean mint.
# 2. **@void/narcissus** — reviewed. Substrate-mode altitude sibling;
#    composition edge declared above.
# 3. **`shards/epistemologic/reality/time.mirror` `timeline`** — the
#    operational carrier for ordered snapshot-sequence at nanosecond
#    substrate. @time/past.peer_history composes over `timeline` at
#    substrate-decl altitude. Sibling altitudes.
# 4. **`shards/song.mirror` prior-beat chain** — the operational
#    surface @time/past reads through. Composition edge declared.
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/time/past.mirror`
# declares `@time/past` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1974
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/math/lagrange-1772
source @arxiv/practice/void-corpus-2026

prism @time/past {
  focus  time_past_state
  project time_past_state
  split  time_past_state
  shift  time_past_state
  settle time_past_state
}

# === time_past_state — the backwards-lens temporal-projection carrier ===
#
# Typed record carrying the backwards-lens temporal-projection state.
# Five fields. Identity contract: byte-equality on the five-field
# tuple.
#
#   observer         — the peer performing the backwards-lens
#                       temporal projection.
#
#   peer_history     — H(t) = {settled Crystal<T> chain of prior
#                       @song/beats the observer's timeline
#                       traversed}. Content-addressed per
#                       `@epistemologic/property/verdict_is_content_
#                       addressed` discipline. Composition-identical
#                       to @void/narcissus.void_narcissus_state.
#                       peer_history.
#
#   saga_ref         — REF to the @song saga the peer_history is
#                       drawn from. Content-addressed. Composition
#                       edge to @song.
#
#   forster_witness  — the Förster-invariant marker; resolves to
#                       `choices_preserved` (healthy) or `choices_
#                       reduced` (Förster violation). The
#                       `past_reading_preserves_choices` bilateral
#                       checks this field.
#
#   timestamp        — monotonic instant per @epistemologic/reality/
#                       time.instant discipline of the observation
#                       event.
type time_past_state = {
  observer:         peer,
  peer_history:     ref,
  saga_ref:         ref,
  forster_witness:  ref,
  timestamp:        ref,
}

# === time_past_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, time_past_state) pair discharge admissibility for
# backwards-lens temporal-projection observation? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.peer_history resolves via content-addressed lookup to a
#     non-empty settled-Crystal-chain (substrate present; no null
#     history)
#   - ctx.saga_ref resolves to a well-formed @song saga
#   - The prior-beats chain in the saga is byte-consistent with
#     ctx.peer_history (Crystal<T> chain matches)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; content-addressed
# resolvability; @song saga resolvability. Sentinel:
# `time=past-admissible`.
bilateral time_past_admissible {
  sentinel "time=past-admissible"
  arity 2
}
time_past_admissible(p: peer, ctx: time_past_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === past_reading_preserves_choices — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, time_past_state) pair discharge the Förster-
# invariant health check? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.forster_witness resolves to `choices_preserved`
#   - The observation event does NOT reduce the choice-set available
#     to peers in the present or future @song/beats (the choice-set
#     is monotonically non-decreasing across the reading)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; choice-set cardinality trace.
# Sentinel: `time=past-forster-invariant`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral IS the Förster-invariant check at
# @time/past altitude. Discharging Fail signals Förster violation
# (narrative-imposition; deterministic-past-forcing); consumers
# MUST treat Fail as substrate-collapse-detected.
bilateral past_reading_preserves_choices {
  sentinel "time=past-forster-invariant"
  arity 2
}
past_reading_preserves_choices(p: peer, ctx: time_past_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === project_backwards — the action ===
#
# Given a peer and a time_past_state, discharge the backwards-lens
# temporal-projection event: read the peer_history H(t) through the
# @song saga; return the projected substrate-mode observation.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the projection
# ref; failure carries not-admissible / forster-violated / saga-
# broken reasons.
#
# Requires BOTH bilateral predicates to discharge Pass.
#
# Sentinel: `time=past-project`.
project_backwards(p: peer, ctx: time_past_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires time_past_admissible(p, ctx)
requires past_reading_preserves_choices(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === Forward-promised (NOT landed this tick) ===
#
# - `pillar::backwards_lens_of_void_narcissus` at Reed's pillar
#   surface — empirical firing already forward-promised by Mara
#   Round-1 math root §10.1; Reed post-Round-2 territory.
# - `pillar::choices_monotone_of_song` empirical firing — the
#   Förster-invariant check at Reed's pillar surface; Alex Q3
#   ratified name; Reed post-Round-2 territory.

out @time/past
out time_past_state
out time_past_admissible
out past_reading_preserves_choices
out project_backwards
